.TH PRISM 1 "" "PRISM" "PRISM Manual"
.SH NAME
prism \- review and safely merge AWS CodeCommit pull requests, and review spec documents, from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prism
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B prism run
.I pr_id
.RB [ \-\-path
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-repo
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-merge ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-d ]
.br
.B prism docs
.I file
\&...
.RB [ \-\-branch
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-persona
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-requirements
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-push ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-d ]
.br
.B prism docs
.B \-\-be
.I file
\&...
.B \-\-fe
.I file
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prism
runs the same review, description and merge pipeline as the PRISM desktop
application, with the same safety checks, but needs no display. Use it locally,
or ssh into the machine that has AWS access and the reviewer engine and review
from anywhere.
.PP
.B prism run
works out what it needs from the folder you are in: the git repository (from
any subdirectory), the CodeCommit repository name and region from its
.B origin
remote, then your saved defaults. A folder that holds several clones needs
.BR \-\-repo ;
PRISM never guesses between them.
.PP
.PP
.B prism docs
reviews requirement\-decomposition documents and specs, the same way the desktop
application's Document review tab does. The reviewer reads the codebase and, when you
give them, the requirements the documents were decomposed from, through the lens of a
chosen persona (Business Analyst, Architect or QA; see
.BR \-\-persona ),
always checking security, stability and scalability. PRISM adds its findings to
the end of each document as a \(lqPRISM review comments\(rq section, grouped by severity
(Blocker, Major, Minor, Suggestion) with a category and a stable id such as
.BR DR\-3 .
The section is written to aid a human review, not to replace it. PRISM then
commits it to the branch as
.B PRISM\-<run id>: <brief message>
and pushes it to
.BR origin ,
never forced. All of this happens in a temporary
.B git worktree
of the branch, so your clone's checked\-out branch, files and uncommitted work are
never changed (as for a pull request review, the reviewer's agent files are
installed under
.I .opencode/
in the project folder). Running it again on the same documents is an incremental review:
the reviewer reports whether each earlier comment is resolved, partly resolved,
still open or withdrawn, then reviews only what changed (it does not re-review the
whole document), and each run is kept as a
numbered version in the same section.
.PP
Every run keeps a record and a log under
.IR ~/.prism/cli\-jobs/ ,
which is how the desktop application lists, stops and retries jobs started here.
The packaged desktop build accepts the same commands, for example
.BR "PRISM run 214" .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "run " pr_id
Review pull request
.IR pr_id .
Runs in the foreground; Ctrl\-C stops it cleanly (twice to leave at once).
.TP
.BI "docs " file ...
Review one or more documents in the repository you are in, on the branch you have
checked out. For a backend and/or frontend use
.B \-\-be
and
.B \-\-fe
instead of plain arguments. Runs in the foreground; Ctrl\-C stops it cleanly.
.TP
.B jobs
List running jobs.
.TP
.BI "logs " id
Show a job's transcript.
.TP
.BI "stop " id
Stop a running job.
.TP
.BI "retry " id
Run a finished job again with the same settings.
.TP
.BI "ask " "id question"
Ask the reviewer about a finished job. Read\-only: nothing is changed or merged.
.TP
.BI "rm " id ...
Delete finished jobs' records and logs.
.TP
.B models
List the reviewer models available.
.TP
.B doctor
Check this machine's setup: git, the AWS CLI and its sign\-in, CodeCommit access, the
review engine and its models. Says how to fix what is wrong. Exits 1 when a check fails.
.TP
.BI "export " id
Save a job's log, settings and a setup check as one .zip file to send for debugging.
Passwords, tokens and webhook URLs are removed first.
.TP
.B repos
Show the git clones PRISM finds in a folder.
.TP
.B config
Show or change saved defaults.
.TP
.B update
Check for a newer release.
.TP
.B man
Install this manual page.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.TP
.B help
Show the built\-in command summary.
.SH OPTIONS FOR RUN
.TP
.BI \-\-path " DIR"
Project folder. Default: the git repository you are in, else the saved
.BR project_dir .
.TP
.BI \-\-repo " NAME"
CodeCommit repository name. Default: saved
.BR repo ,
else the clone's remote, else the folder's name.
.TP
.BI \-\-clone " DIR"
Local clone to use when it is not the folder itself.
.TP
.BI \-\-region " REGION"
AWS region. Default: saved
.BR region ,
else the remote's region, else us\-east\-1.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " NAME"
Reviewer model; see
.BR "prism models" .
.TP
.BR \-\-review ", " \-\-no\-review
Run the review (default), or skip it and only sync and merge.
.TP
.BR \-\-describe ", " \-\-no\-describe
Write the findings into the PR description (default), or not. Always off
without a review.
.TP
.BR \-\-merge ", " \-\-no\-merge
Merge on approval (default), or review only.
.TP
.BR \-\-sync ", " \-\-no\-sync
Sync the destination branch into the source first (default), or not.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Review, but change nothing in AWS or git.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-instructions " \fITEXT\fR"
Extra instructions for the reviewer.
.TP
.BI \-\-instructions\-file " FILE"
Read the extra instructions from a file.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-detach
Run in the background and return; the job survives logging out.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print nothing. The log is still kept.
.PP
A flag always beats a saved default.
.SH OPTIONS FOR DOCS
Documents are named as you would to a shell: relative to where you are, absolute,
or, for a file that exists only on the branch, from the repository root.
.TP
.I file ...
Document(s) to review, in a single repository: the one you are in, or
.BR \-\-clone .
.TP
.BI \-\-path " DIR"
Project folder. Default: the git repository you are in, else the saved
.BR project_dir .
.TP
.BI \-\-clone " DIR"
The repository's clone, when it is not the folder itself.
.TP
.BI \-\-branch " NAME"
Branch the documents are on. Default: the branch checked out in the clone. A
detached HEAD needs this.
.TP
.BI \-\-be " FILE" ...
Documents in the backend repository. Use with
.BR \-\-fe ,
or alone. Not together with plain
.I file
arguments.
.TP
.BI \-\-be\-clone " DIR"
The backend clone. Default: the one among the clones under the project folder
whose name says backend (\fIbe\fR, \fIbackend\fR), or the other of two when only
the frontend is named. Never guessed between clones that do not say which is which.
.TP
.BI \-\-be\-branch " NAME"
Backend branch. Default: the one checked out.
.TP
.BI \-\-fe " FILE" ...
Documents in the frontend repository.
.TP
.BI \-\-fe\-clone " DIR"
The frontend clone; found the same way as the backend one.
.TP
.BI \-\-fe\-branch " NAME"
Frontend branch. Default: the one checked out.
.TP
.BI \-\-persona " NAME"
Who reviews, each through its own lens. Default: saved
.BR persona ,
else
.BR ba .
.RS
.TP
.B ba
Business Analyst, the functional side: do the document's functional requirements align
with the requirements (when given) and with themselves, and match what the codebase
actually does?
.TP
.B architect
the technical side: the codebase's existing patterns against what the document
proposes. Is the proposal valid, and does it lead to security loopholes, bugs or
inconsistencies with those patterns?
.TP
.B qa
the quality side: will implementing this break anything, how does it affect the quality
of the product, and can it be tested?
.RE
.IP
Security, stability and scalability are always checked, whichever persona is chosen,
and the review states its conclusion on each. Each persona's reviews are tracked
separately: running the Architect again follows up the Architect's earlier comments.
.TP
.BI \-\-requirements " DIR"
Optional. The folder holding the requirements the documents were decomposed from.
Default: saved
.BR requirements ,
else none. With it the review centres on whether the decomposition satisfies the entire
requirement, and is consistent with the codebase's patterns. Without it, it centres on
whether the documents are consistent with the codebase's patterns and the design is good
to implement without breaking anything. A relative path is read from the reviewed branch
of each repository (then from the project folder); a folder you can see from where you
are is stored relative to the repository it lies in. A path that is given but not found
is an error.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " NAME"
Reviewer model; see
.BR "prism models" .
.TP
.BR \-\-commit ", " \-\-no\-commit
Commit the review comments to the branch (default), or leave nothing behind.
Without a commit nothing is kept: the review exists only in the log.
.TP
.BR \-\-push ", " \-\-no\-push
Push the commit to the remote (default). Needs a commit. If the branch moved on
the remote, PRISM replays its one commit on top and pushes again; if that fails
the commit is kept as
.I refs/prism/docs/<run id>\-<role>
in the clone and nothing is lost.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Review, but write, commit and push nothing.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-instructions " \fITEXT\fR"
Extra instructions for the reviewer.
.TP
.BI \-\-instructions\-file " FILE"
Read the extra instructions from a file.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-detach
Run in the background and return; the job survives logging out.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print nothing. The log is still kept.
.PP
A flag always beats a saved default.
.SH OTHER OPTIONS
.TP
.B jobs \-a, \-\-all
Include finished jobs.
.TP
.B jobs \-\-json
Machine\-readable output.
.TP
.B logs \-f, \-\-follow
Keep following until the job ends.
.TP
.B logs \-n, \-\-lines \fIN\fR
Only the last N lines.
.TP
.B stop \-\-all
Stop every running CLI job.
.TP
.B retry \-d, \-q
Detach, or run quietly. Works for document reviews too.
.TP
.B rm \-\-all
Delete every finished job.
.TP
.B models \-\-refresh
Ask the engine again instead of using the cached list.
.TP
.B doctor \-\-repo \fIDIR\fR, \-\-pr \fIID\fR, \-\-region \fIREGION\fR, \-\-model \fINAME\fR
Also test the clone (can it fetch from origin), the pull request (can PRISM read it),
the region, and that the model exists. Use the values of the job that failed.
.TP
.B doctor \-\-quick
Only look at this machine: no network or engine calls.
.TP
.B doctor \-\-json
Machine\-readable output.
.TP
.B doctor \-o \fIFILE\fR, \-\-output \fIFILE\fR
Also save the report to a .zip.
.TP
.B export \-o \fIFILE\fR, \-\-output \fIFILE\fR
Where to save the .zip (default: the current folder).
.TP
.B export \-\-no\-checks
Leave out the network setup checks (faster, less useful).
.TP
.B update \-\-install
Download and install a newer release (packaged builds only).
.TP
.B man \-\-install, \-\-dir \fIDIR\fR, \-\-path
Install the manual page (default directory
.IR ~/.local/share/man/man1 ),
or print where it is.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Defaults live in
.I ~/.prism/config.json
(the file the desktop application also uses) under a
.B cli
key:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
  "cli": {
    "project_dir": "/home/me/work",
    "repo": "my\-service",
    "region": "eu\-west\-1",
    "model": "anthropic/claude\-sonnet\-5\-5",
    "instructions": "Flag missing tests",
    "requirements": "docs/requirements",
    "persona": "architect",
    "review": true,
    "describe": true,
    "merge": false,
    "sync": true,
    "dry_run": false,
    "commit": true,
    "push": true
  },
  "google_chat_webhook_url": "https://chat.googleapis.com/..."
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Text keys are
.BR project_dir ,
.BR repo ,
.BR region ,
.BR model ,
.BR instructions ,
.B requirements
and
.BR persona ;
an empty value means "not set". Yes/no keys are
.BR review ,
.BR describe ,
.BR merge ,
.B sync
and
.BR dry_run ,
which
.B prism run
reads, and
.B commit
and
.BR push ,
which
.B prism docs
reads.
.BR model ,
.B instructions
and
.B dry_run
apply to both commands, and
.BR requirements ,
.B persona
(\fBba\fR, \fBarchitect\fR or \fBqa\fR),
.B commit
and
.B push
are only for documents.
Edit the file by hand or use:
.PP
.RS
.B prism config
.br
.B prism config set
.I key value
.br
.B prism config unset
.I key
.br
.B prism config path
.RE
.PP
The extra key
.B webhook
sets the Google Chat webhook shared with the desktop application.
.SH QUESTIONS
In a terminal, PRISM asks you directly when it needs an answer (merge conflicts,
the confirmation for a high\-impact merge). A detached or non\-interactive job
has nobody to ask and takes the cautious answer: conflicts are not resolved and
a high\-impact merge is not confirmed.
.PP
A document review can also stop and ask you something when it cannot review
without the answer (which of two requirement folders is authoritative, for
example). In a terminal you answer on the spot; a detached run has nobody to ask
and carries on without an answer.
.SH EXAMPLES
Review PR 214 of the repository in the current folder:
.PP
.RS
prism run 214
.RE
.PP
Review only, without merging, in the background, then follow it:
.PP
.RS
prism run 214 \-\-no\-merge \-d
.br
prism logs 7f3a9c \-f
.RE
.PP
Review a spec in the repository you are in, on the branch you have checked out:
.PP
.RS
prism docs docs/spec.md
.RE
.PP
Review two documents on a named branch, without pushing, then look at the result:
.PP
.RS
prism docs docs/spec.md docs/decomposition.md \-\-branch feat/specs \-\-no\-push
.RE
.PP
Review a spec as the Architect, against the codebase alone (no requirements given):
.PP
.RS
prism docs docs/spec.md \-\-persona architect
.RE
.PP
Review it as QA against its requirements:
.PP
.RS
prism docs docs/spec.md \-\-persona qa \-\-requirements docs/requirements
.RE
.PP
Backend and frontend documents in one run, requirements kept elsewhere, in the
background:
.PP
.RS
cd ~/work    # holds shop\-backend and shop\-frontend
.br
prism docs \-\-be docs/spec.md \-\-fe docs/ui\-spec.md \-\-requirements docs/reqs \-d
.br
prism logs 7f3a9c \-f
.RE
.PP
Review again after the author's edits, then ask about a comment:
.PP
.RS
prism retry 7f3a9c
.br
prism ask 7f3a9c why is DR\-2 a blocker
.RE
.PP
Set defaults once:
.PP
.RS
prism config set region eu\-west\-1
.br
prism config set model anthropic/claude\-sonnet\-5\-5
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (a finished review, merged or not).
.TP
.B 1
The job failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, or the same pull request or documents are already being reviewed.
.TP
.B 130
The job was stopped.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.prism/config.json
Saved settings.
.TP
.I ~/.prism/cli\-jobs/
A record (\fIid\fR.json), log (\fIid\fR.log) and stop request (\fIid\fR.stop) per job.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns off coloured output.
.SH SEE ALSO
The README and docs/MANUAL.md in the PRISM repository.
